[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_s")
id = "wrath"
display_name = "The earth's wrath"
title = "The earth's wrath"
category = "The Earth"
order = 53
image = "res://art/guide/wrath.png"
body = "The road is alive and it keeps a ledger. Kill enough of what lives out here - and the rarer the animal, the sharper the cost - burn enough forest, fell enough timber, lean hard enough on one element, and the land begins to answer.

You are never shown a number for this, and you never will be. What you get are signs: the birds go quiet, the ground will not settle, the sky goes strange. Each is said once, when the anger climbs a step. Learn them.

A living legendary animal is an anchor - while one is out there the land is calmer, and hazards come more slowly. Killing it is a real reward, a real shock, and the loss of that calm for the rest of the run.

Nothing you do reduces the anger. Only the absence of the things that raise it: leave the road quiet for a while and it eases, slowly."
